subject: fix(smart-router): pass credentials when fetching custom node /models

BUG: The smart router could not discover models from auth-gated custom
provider nodes (e.g. Dialagram). getNodeModels() called /models without
any auth header, got 401, returned empty candidate list, and the router
fell through to built-in providers (openai) which had no credentials.
The request failed with "No active credentials for provider: openai"
even though the user had a valid custom provider configured.

Direct curl to Dialagram confirmed:
  - Without auth: HTTP 401
  - With Bearer token: HTTP 200, returns 15 models

ROOT CAUSE: The dashboard /api/providers/[id]/models/route.js already
passes Authorization: Bearer ${connection.apiKey} for custom nodes, but
the smart router getNodeModels() never replicated that pattern. This
was an oversight from the original custom-node support commit (8990a3b4).

FIX (src/sse/services/smartRouter.js):
1. Added getProviderConnections import from @/lib/localDb
2. New getNodeApiKey(nodeId) helper finds the first active connection
   for a node and returns its apiKey (highest priority)
3. getNodeModels() now builds auth headers based on node type:
   - openai-compatible: Authorization: Bearer <apiKey>
   - anthropic-compatible: x-api-key + Authorization Bearer
4. Fail-open preserved: if no connection exists or fetch fails, returns
   [] and the router silently skips that node

VERIFICATION (production build, port 20130, Dialagram live provider):
- Before: modelRouter -> "No active credentials for provider: openai"
- After: modelRouter -> Dialagram/nexum-router -> real code response
- Direct dialagram/qwen-3.5-plus: works
- dialagram/nexum-router: works (Dialagram own internal router)

This makes smart router custom-node support ACTUALLY work for auth-gated
third-party routers (Dialagram, OpenRouter self-hosted, any OpenAI-
compatible gateway behind an API key).

Related: 8990a3b4 (initial custom node), 429ddc56, 6449b58b
Part of: Smart Router & Fallback UX plan (M1 custom-node completion)

